<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santiago de Querétaro</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Querétaro City</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> de Querétaro is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> and the capital of the state of Querétaro. Founded in 1531 as an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otomi">Otomi</a> and Spanish town, it grew into a wealthy colonial centre whose historic core is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>. Emperor Maximilian was besieged and captured there in 1867, and the Mexican Constitution of 1917 was drafted and signed in the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santiago-de-queretaro.jpg" alt="Santiago de Querétaro" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Microstar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panor%C3%A1mica_Jard%C3%ADn_Zenea.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
